{"id": "EUVD-2026-103038", "enisaUuid": "dc658793-a9db-30a6-8109-ac0af11162d4", "description": "Oqtane Framework through 10.2.6 contains an authorization bypass vulnerability in SettingController that allows a site administrator to read another co-tenant site's private settings. Attackers with the Administrators role on one site can request another site's entityId through their own alias to retrieve stored SMTPPassword and SMTPClientSecret values.", "datePublished": "2026-10-16T17:38:54", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T21:19:35", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:H/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@hieuPenguinnn/oqtane-setting-site-cross-site-private-settings-idor", "https://github.com/oqtane/oqtane.framework/blob/v10.2.6/Oqtane.Server/Controllers/SettingController.cs#L411-L516", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/oqtane-framework-through-10.2.6-cross-site-settings-disclosure-via-setting-api"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111616", "GHSA-cc9f-f98j-3ppq"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.35, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "a8be9818-b3f3-3be2-bb2e-a28d714f6246", "product": {"name": "Oqtane Framework", "vendor": {"name": "Oqtane"}}, "product_version": "0 \u226410.2.6"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "0c8b6409-bd1e-3d5c-9791-5f9f9abe6167", "vendor": {"name": "Oqtane"}}], "isExploited": false}